{"name":"Graceful Garden","hex":"#cba9d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"graceful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having or showing grace in movement, shape, or proportion.","Magnanimous, lacking arrogance or complaint; gracious."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graceful"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gracefulness","blocks":[{"text":"Gracefulness, or being graceful, is the physical characteristic of displaying \"pretty agility\", in the form of elegant movement, poise, or balance. The etymological root of grace is the Latin word gratia from gratus, meaning pleasing. Gracefulness has been described by reference to its being aesthetically pleasing. For example:"},{"text":"Gracefulness is an idea not very different from beauty; it consists of much the same things. Gracefulness is an idea belonging to posture and motion. In both these, to be graceful, it is requisite that there be no appearance of difficulty; there is required a small inflection of the body; and a composure of the parts in such a manner, as not to encumber each other, not to appear divided by sharp and sudden angles. In this ease, this roundness, this delicacy of attitude and motion, it is that all the magic of grace consists, and what is called its je ne sais quoi; as will be obvious to any observer, who considers attentively the Venus de Medicis, the Antinous, or any statue generally allowed to be graceful in an high degree."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Swan_-_Harrold_Country_Park_October_2009_%284061559567%29.jpg/330px-Swan_-_Harrold_Country_Park_October_2009_%284061559567%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gracefulness"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg/500px-Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg/1280px-Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg/500px-Ballet-Ballerina-1853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Like swans, ballerinas are often used as an examples of gracefulness.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABallet-Ballerina-1853.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/500px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/1280px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg/500px-Cerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"graceful\" Japanese cherry tree.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACerisier_du_Japon_Prunus_serrulata.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/500px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/1280px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/500px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The New Jersey Botanical Garden at Skylands Estate","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkylands3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG/500px-%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG/500px-%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Partial view from the Botanical Garden of Curitiba (Southern Brazil): parterres, flowers, fountains, sculptures, greenhouses and tracks composes the place used for recreation and to study and protect the flora.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A'JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped